SSIS Documentation 
🔷 1. Overall Architecture

Your ETL solution consists of 3 main packages:

Master_ETL
Orchestrates execution
Controls flow & batching
Load_Dimensions
Loads all dimension tables
Uses full + incremental strategies
Load_Facts
Loads fact tables
Uses incremental loading with business logic
🧱 2. Package: Load_Dimensions
🔹 Purpose

Handles all dimension tables (lookup + descriptive data)

Examples:

Customer
Product
Category
Warehouse
etc.
🔹 Design Pattern
🟢 1. Full Load (Static Dimensions)

Used for:

Small tables
Rarely changing data
Flow:
TRUNCATE → Reload (DFT)
🔄 2. Incremental Load (Slowly Changing Data)

For larger dimensions like:

Customer
Product
Pattern:
Get Last Load
   ↓
Extract new/updated records
   ↓
Transform
   ↓
Load into DW
   ↓
Update Control Table
🔹 Likely Transformations Used
Lookup (to detect existing records)
Derived Column (data formatting)
Conditional Split (new vs existing)
Possibly SCD logic (Type 1)
🔹 Key Concept

👉 This package separates:

Static dimensions → Full reload
Dynamic dimensions → Incremental

💡 This is exactly how real DW systems work

📦 3. Package: Load_Facts
🔹 Purpose

Handles fact tables (transactions/measures)

Examples:

Sales
Orders
Inventory movements
🔹 Core Logic (VERY IMPORTANT 🚨)

Fact tables are always:

✅ Incremental ONLY (never full reload)

🔄 Pattern Used
Get Last Successful Load
        ↓
Extract new transactions
        ↓
Lookup Dimension Keys (Surrogate Keys)
        ↓
Transform Measures
        ↓
Load into Fact Table
        ↓
Update Control Table
🔹 Critical Step: Dimension Lookups

Before loading facts:

👉 You map:

Business keys → Surrogate keys

Example:

CustomerID → CustomerKey
ProductID → ProductKey

💡 This is the heart of Data Warehousing

🔹 Transformations You Likely Used
Lookup (for dimension keys)
Derived Column (calculations)
Data conversion
Conditional Split (valid vs rejected)
🔹 Data Integrity Handling
Reject unmatched records
Or redirect errors

👉 This is important for:

Data quality
Referential integrity
🔗 4. How Everything Works Together
Execution Flow:
Master_ETL
    ↓
Load_Dimensions
    ↓
Load_Facts
    ↓
Finalize Batch
🧠 Logical Order (Correct Design ✔)
Load Dimensions first
Then load Facts

👉 Because facts depend on dimension keys

🔥 5. Advanced Features You Implemented

Your project includes:

✅ Control Table System
Tracks last load per table
Enables incremental loading
✅ Batch Processing
Open batch
Process data
Close batch
✅ Domain Separation
Customer domain
Inventory domain
✅ Reusable Pattern

Same ETL logic applied across tables
